    <text>
        <body>
            <div type="edition" xml:space="preserve">
                <ab>
                   <lb n="1"/>Ἐ<hi rend="ligature">ν πρ</hi>ώτοις
                   <lb n="2"/><hi rend="ligature">μνή</hi>σθητι
                   <lb n="3"/><persName type="divine" key="Christ"><expan><abbr>κ</abbr><ex>ύρι</ex>ε</expan></persName> τ<hi rend="ligature">οῦ</hi> <term type="office" ref="of0218"><hi rend="ligature">ἀρ</hi>χι
                   <lb n="4" break="no"/>ἐπισκόπ<hi rend="ligature">ου</hi></term> <hi rend="ligature">ἡμ</hi>ῶν
                   <lb n="5"/><persName type="attested" ref="#pers48">Ἱερεμίου</persName>
                   <lb n="6"/>ὸν χάρισαι
                   <lb n="7"/>ταῖς <hi rend="ligature">ἁγ</hi>ίαις
                   <lb n="8"/>ἐκκλησίαις.
                </ab>
            </div>
            <div type="apparatus">
                <p>The text is part of the standard intercessory prayer recited to commemorate the patriarchs of Constantinople during the liturgy. The full text is as follows: "Ἐν πρώτοις μνήσθητι, Κύριε, τοῦ Ἀρχιεπισκόπου ἡμῶν Ἱερεμίου, ὃν χάρισαι ταῖς ἁγίαις σου Ἐκκλησίαις ἐν εἰρήνῃ, σῷον, ἔντιμον, ὑγιᾶ, μακροημερεύοντα καὶ ὀρθοτομοῦντα τὸν λόγον τῆς σῆς ἀληθείας".</p>
            </div>
            <div type="translation">
                <p>Remember Lord among the first our Archbishop Jeremias, whom grant to thy holy churches [in peace ...] (Chatzidakis, Cretan Painter, 49).</p>
            </div>
            <div type="commentary">
                <p></p>
            </div>
            <div type="bibliography">
                <p>Chatzidakis, Cretan Painter.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
